From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri.3012@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:12:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: core support for the AC-PHY

The b43 core for the AC-PHY cores (core rev 42, BCM4352 and BCM4360):
what the core does differently outside the PHY. Built with
CONFIG_B43_PHY_AC. The AC cores use the DMA, RX, TX and TX status paths
of the N/HT series before this patch, with branches for the AC only:

- DMA: the AC core's RX header and buffer size, the 256-slot RX ring of
  the N/HT cores, and the engine's burst and prefetch settings from core
  rev 40. A DMA64 engine that takes unaligned rings is detected once per
  device and logged; only the AC cores use it, with descriptor addresses
  in the index registers and the RX index one descriptor short, as
  brcmsmac's dma64_rxfill() keeps one back;
- TX: the 128-byte AC TX header, A-MPDUs aggregated by the AC microcode
  (one TX status per A-MPDU, acks from its block ack bitmap), A-MSDUs
  built by mac80211 (TX_AMSDU), transmit beamforming (off unless the
  txbf module parameter is set);
- RX: the AC's rate decoding and the A-MSDU pieces it splits off, put
  back together before mac80211 sees them;
- hardware keys of the AC core's key table;
- AP: beacons and their PHY TX control, several BSSes on one radio, and
  the radar handling behind CONFIG_B43_DFS;
- LEDs: pins 4-15 from the board's NVRAM, driven from the ChipCommon;
- Kconfig: B43_PHY_AC and B43_DFS.

From b43-ac-wip 7bc6476, rebased onto the N/HT series.

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri.3012@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
